{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTModuliUnderdetermined","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTModuliUnderdetermined","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dt_moduliDim_underdetermined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dt_moduliDim_underdetermined","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTModuliUnderdetermined.lean#L101-L119","doc":"**THE CRUX (limitative).**  The `Δ_λ = Behrend-signed DT-count` target\nUNDER-DETERMINES the moduli dimension: two DISTINCT moduli-dimension\nassignments — the Springer value `n(λ)` and `n(λ)+2` — both realize `Δ_λ`\nwith the substrate count `dim V_λ`.  So matching `Δ_λ` constrains the moduli\ndimension only *mod 2* (its Behrend-sign parity), never the actual Springer\nvalue `n(λ) = dim_ℂ 𝓑_λ`.  The `Δ_λ = DT-count` identification therefore does\nNOT force the Springer fibre `𝓑_λ`; the dimension `n(λ)` must come from an\nindependent substrate map (the a-function / GS jet-order valuation).  This is\nthe precise sense in which the toy `moduliDim := nStat` merely READS the\nanswer — the open internal derivation (`DeltaLambdaDTRealization`, bean\n`qou-ylot`) is not closed by the DT identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dt_moduliDim_sign_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dt_moduliDim_sign_forced","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTModuliUnderdetermined.lean#L86-L99","doc":"**Count forced up to sign; sign forced.**  Any DT realization that uses the\nsubstrate count `vc = dim V_λ` has its Behrend sign `(-1)^{md λ}` pinned to\n`(-1)^{n(λ)}` — the target `Δ_λ` determines the parity of the moduli\ndimension exactly.  (The count itself is `dim V_λ` by the landed\n`binding_magnitude_eq_dim`; here we isolate the sign leg.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.shifted_dt_realization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.shifted_dt_realization","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTModuliUnderdetermined.lean#L78-L84","doc":"**The parity-shifted reading ALSO realizes `Δ_λ`.**  Bumping the moduli\ndimension by `2` leaves the Behrend sign `(-1)^{md}` unchanged, so\n`md = n(λ)+2` with the same count reproduces every `Δ_λ`.  This is the\nwitness that the moduli dimension is not pinned by the `Δ_λ` target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonical_dt_realization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonical_dt_realization","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTModuliUnderdetermined.lean#L71-L76","doc":"**The Springer/toy reading realizes `Δ_λ`.**  `md = n(λ)` (a-function =\n`dim_ℂ 𝓑_λ`), `vc = dim V_λ` (Wedderburn count) reproduces every `Δ_λ` — this\nis `deltaSign_eq_nStat_parity` repackaged as a DT realization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsDTRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsDTRealization","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTModuliUnderdetermined.lean#L68-L69","signatureChunk":0}]}